# Typo coverage

This document deliberately uses misspelled keys to pin Taliesin's schema validators.
Each unknown key below produces one click-to-source warning; rendering is unaffected.

The front matter covers three *different* mistakes on purpose, because they need three
different messages: a **typo** gets a did-you-mean (`langg`, `cach`, `max-itemz`), a name
with no near neighbour gets no guess at all rather than a wrong one (`theorems:` is far
from every live key, so the distance rule declines), and a **recognized but inert** key
gets neither, because there is nothing to rename (`csl:` parses, and has never had an
effect). An unknown PARENT key takes its children with it: nothing below `theorems:` is
validated, because the block itself names nothing.

::: {.callout-warnign}
This callout names a kind Taliesin does not define.
:::

::: {.column-margn}
This div names a feature class Taliesin does not define; it silently degraded before DX5.
:::

